   "properties": {
    "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
   },
   "widgets_values": [
    "# Image to video (Wan 2.2)\n\n1. **Pick your image** in the green *Load Image* box.\n2. **Write the motion** in the green *Your prompt* box, like \"she turns her head and smiles\".\n3. Set **width and height** in *Video size* to match your image: 480 x 832 for portrait, 832 x 480 for landscape.\n4. Click the blue **Run** button at the top of the screen.\n5. The video shows in *Result* and is saved to `ComfyUI/output/video`.\n\n**Speed:** about 10 minutes for this 3-second clip on this Mac. Close other heavy apps first, because video uses nearly all the memory, and keep at least 40 GB of disk free.\n\n**Length** is in frames at 16 per second, and must be 4n+1: 33 = 2s, 49 = 3s, 81 = 5s.\n\n**NSFW LoRA:** there are two, high and low. Keep both at the same strength. Put the trigger word `nsfwsks` in your prompt to activate them.\n\nLeave the 4 steps alone: the speed LoRAs are built for exactly that.\n"
   ]
  },
